Had a lovely dinner at Amore Italiano. We ordered cannelloni, vegetarian soup, vegetariana pizza, tiramisu, and profiteroles—each dish was well-prepared and delicious. The flavors were comforting and authentic, especially the pizza which had a nice thin crust and generous toppings. The desserts were a sweet finish, with the tiramisu being rich and creamy, and the profiteroles light and satisfying. The place had a warm, cozy vibe that made the dining experience even better. Definitely a spot I’d recommend for a relaxed Italian meal.

